        "id": 1045980
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-06T20:49:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like other bpfs just use a u32 in place of a pointer, and then have some is_valid_access/convert_ctx_access magic to turn it back into a pointer. We can do something similar.",
      "parentUuid": "6a5bbce8_611718b3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1015,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1015,
        "endChar": 19
